<?php

namespace App\Libraries;

/**
 * Seventh batch (300+ entries): the NEXUS-L InterLink background service (the C# tray program, its installer, queue,
 * sign-in and troubleshooting), the Admin-only Settings page (service, report defaults, approval link, Synology, database
 * switch and transfer), the approval-then-send flow, Add / Edit mode, the reading pages of every test, and the Report Detail
 * page. No secret (key, token, password) and no threshold is written here. Loaded by `php spark brain:seed`.
 */
class BrainSeed7
{
    /** @return list<array<string,mixed>> */
    public static function all(): array
    {
        $o = static fn (string $label, string $url): array => ['type' => 'open', 'label' => $label, 'url' => $url];
        $k = static fn (string $title, string $keywords, string $body, array $steps = [], array $extra = []): array => array_merge(['title' => $title, 'keywords' => $keywords, 'body' => $body, 'steps' => $steps], $extra);
        $il    = ['page_match' => 'interlink'];
        $st    = ['page_match' => 'settings', 'role_min' => 'admin'];
        $adm   = ['role_min' => 'admin'];
        $goIl  = ['actions' => [$o('Open InterLink Sync', 'interlink')]];
        $goSt  = ['actions' => [$o('Open Settings', 'settings')]];

        return [
            // =========================================================== The service: what it is (30)
            $k('What is the NEXUS-L InterLink Service?', 'interlink service, nexus interlink service, what is the service, c# service, background service, interlink background service, tray program', 'A small Windows program (a tray icon next to the clock) that receives an approved report from NEXUS-L and submits it to InterLink in the background with an invisible browser. Nobody has to open InterLink, fill boxes or attach the PDF: NEXUS-L sends the payload and the signed PDF, the service does Add or Edit in InterLink and reports back.', [], $il + $goIl),
            $k('How does a report get from NEXUS-L to InterLink now?', 'how report reaches interlink, flow nexus to interlink, send flow, report path interlink, how does sending work', 'You press Send in NEXUS-L. NEXUS-L checks the report is approved and signed, builds the payload and the signed PDF and hands them to the service. The service puts the job in its queue, fills the InterLink Upload Form with an invisible browser, saves it, checks that InterLink really kept it, and calls NEXUS-L back. You get a toast and a Synology message with the result.', [], $il),
            $k('Do I still need the Chrome extension?', 'extension still needed, need chrome extension, sender extension needed, extension or service, do i need the sender', 'Not when the service is set up and answering: it does the sending. The NEXUS-L InterLink Sender extension stays as a fallback; if the service does not answer, NEXUS-L tells you and uses the extension instead (when it is installed).', [], $il),
            $k('What is the difference between the service and the extension?', 'service vs extension, difference service extension, which is better, service or sender, extension versus service', 'The extension works in your own Chrome with your own InterLink sign-in and needs your computer and browser tab. The service runs on one computer in the background with one shared InterLink account and an invisible browser, takes many users\' reports in order, and needs nobody to keep a tab open. Both use the same page logic.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the service open anything on my computer?', 'service opens window, invisible browser, headless browser, service visible, does anything open', 'No. The browser it drives is invisible and runs on the computer where the service is installed, not on yours. You only see a toast in NEXUS-L and a Synology message.', [], $il),
            $k('Which InterLink account does the service use?', 'service account interlink, which account service uses, shared account, interlink login service, submitted under whose name', 'One shared service account, signed in once on the service computer. Everything the service submits goes into InterLink under that account.', [], $il),
            $k('Is the service allowed to send an unapproved report?', 'unapproved report send, send without approval, service approval check, signed report required, approval before send', 'No. Only a report approved and signed by a Manager or Supervisor is sent. NEXUS-L checks it when it builds the job, and the service asks NEXUS-L again right before it presses Save.', [], $il),
            $k('Where does the service run?', 'where service runs, service computer, which pc service, install location service, service on server', 'On one Windows computer that can reach both the NEXUS-L server and InterLink, with Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge installed. It stays running (tray icon) and starts with Windows when you tick that option.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the tray icon of the service mean?', 'tray icon, icon next to clock, notification area icon, service icon, system tray nexus', 'The icon next to the clock means the service is running. Double-click it (or right-click) for Settings, Sign in to InterLink, the Activity window, the Log, and Exit.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the right-click menu of the tray icon contain?', 'tray menu items, right click tray, service menu, tray options, menu of the tray icon', 'Settings..., Sign in to InterLink..., Activity (what is waiting and running), Open the log, and Exit. Double-click opens the properties window.', [], $il),
            $k('How many reports does the service send at the same time?', 'one at a time, concurrent jobs, parallel sending, how many at once, simultaneous reports', 'One at a time. All users share one InterLink session, so the reports wait in a queue and are done in the order they arrived.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the service work when my computer is off?', 'service when pc off, computer off sending, service needs my pc, offline sending, shutdown service', 'It does not depend on your computer. It depends on the computer where the service is installed: that one must be on and the program running.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the service need installed?', 'service requirements, what does service need, prerequisites service, chrome required service, requirements interlink service', 'Windows 10/11 64-bit and Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge. The installer program already contains everything else, so .NET does not have to be installed separately.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the service need an internet connection?', 'service internet, service network, reach interlink service, connection requirements', 'Yes: the service computer must reach InterLink on the internet and the NEXUS-L server on the local network.', [], $il),
            $k('Is my own Chrome profile touched by the service?', 'service chrome profile, profile touched, my chrome signins safe, service uses my chrome, own profile', 'No. The service uses its own clean browser profile in its data folder. Your Chrome profile, bookmarks and sign-ins are not read or changed.', [], $il),
            $k('Which version of the service is this?', 'service version, which version service, version number service, health version', 'The version is shown in the Settings window title and by the Check button, and the health address of the service returns it. Ask an administrator to open Settings > InterLink service > Check.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Who made the service?', 'who made service, credits service, publisher service, credited by, author interlink sender', 'Nexus-L InterLink Sender, credited by Systems & Process Audit. The installer shows this on its first page.', [], []),
            $k('Is the service free to install on more computers?', 'install on more computers, second service computer, many installs, multiple services, more than one service', 'It can be installed on another computer, but NEXUS-L sends to one service address at a time (set in Settings). Two services on the same InterLink account would also compete for one session, so keep one active.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What happens to a report when the service is busy?', 'service busy, report waiting service, queued report busy, wait in line, busy queue', 'It waits in the queue. You are told how many reports are ahead of yours, and you get a second message when it starts and a third when it finishes.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I watch the service work?', 'watch service work, see the browser, visible browser test, show browser, debug service', 'Yes, for testing: in the service Settings untick the invisible browser option, Save and restart. The browser window then shows each step. Tick it again for normal use.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does the Activity window show?', 'activity window, activity list, what is running, service activity, running jobs window', 'The jobs that are waiting or running now, in order, who sent them and the report number. Open it from the tray icon menu.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the Log window show?', 'log window, service log, log list, view log, open the log', 'The history of what the service did: jobs received, steps, InterLink messages, results and errors. It is also stored as data\\service.log next to the program.', [], $il),
            $k('Where are the service files kept?', 'service files location, data folder service, service data folder, where saved queue, service storage', 'Next to the program: appsettings.Local.json (your settings), and the data folder with the saved InterLink sign-in, the queue, the history, the log and the last pictures.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does the service keep a history of jobs?', 'job history, history of sent reports, service history, past jobs, history file', 'Yes. Finished jobs are written to data\\history.jsonl and the recent ones are shown in the Activity window.', [], $il),
            $k('What pictures does the service keep?', 'service pictures, screenshots service, shots folder, pictures of upload form, keep screenshots', 'After Save it takes a picture of the Upload Form, and a picture of the page where a job stopped. The last 40 are kept in data\\shots, which helps to see what InterLink showed.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can two people send reports at the same time?', 'two users at once, many users send, colleagues send same time, concurrent users', 'Yes. Both reports go into the queue and are done one after the other; each person gets their own messages.', [], $il),
            $k('Is the report PDF sent to InterLink signed?', 'signed pdf interlink, signature on pdf, signed attachment, approved pdf sent, which pdf is sent', 'Yes. The service attaches the approved and signed report PDF that NEXUS-L prepared for that report.', [], $il),
            $k('What happens after InterLink keeps the report?', 'after save interlink, what after submit, result after save, done message, finish job', 'The service checks the InterLink search grid shows the Report No. for the application, calls NEXUS-L back, and NEXUS-L shows a toast and sends a Synology message "Labreference / ReportNO / submitted to InterLink".', [], $il),
            $k('Will I be told if sending fails?', 'told if fails, failure message, notice failure, why failed message, failed notification', 'Yes. You get a toast and a Synology message with the reason (for example sign in again, report number already used, or InterLink refused a box).', [], $il),
            $k('What is the shared key?', 'shared key, service key, x-service-key, secret key service, what is key', 'A secret of 16 or more characters that NEXUS-L and the service both know. The service refuses any request that does not carry it. It is set in the service Settings and in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can anyone on the network use the service?', 'service security, anyone use service, public service, secure service, network access service', 'Only a caller with the shared key is accepted, and only an approved, signed report is submitted. Allow its port in the Windows firewall only from the NEXUS-L server.', [], $il + $adm),

            // =========================================================== Install and installer (30)
            $k('How do I install the NEXUS-L InterLink Service?', 'install service, install interlink service, setup service, installer service, how to install the service, nexusinterlinkservice-setup', 'Run NexusInterlinkService-Setup-1.1.0.exe on the service computer. It needs no administrator rights and takes about a minute.', ['Double-click NexusInterlinkService-Setup-1.1.0.exe.', 'Read the first page (Nexus-L InterLink Sender, credited by Systems & Process Audit) and press Next.', 'Keep the folder, tick Start with Windows (and a desktop shortcut if you like).', 'Press Install, then Finish with Start ticked.', 'Open the tray icon > Settings, then sign in to InterLink once.'], $il),
            $k('Where does the installer put the service?', 'install folder, installation path, where installed, default folder service, program location', 'By default in %LocalAppData%\\Programs\\NexusInterlinkService for the current user, with a Start menu entry. You can choose another folder on the installer\'s folder page.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the installer need administrator rights?', 'installer admin rights, administrator install, uac installer, install without admin, run as administrator', 'No. It installs for the current Windows user only and does not ask for administrator rights.', [], $il),
            $k('How big is the installer?', 'installer size, setup size, how big setup, mb installer, download size', 'About 62 MB. The program inside is about 230 MB after installing, because it contains its own runtime so nothing else has to be installed.', [], $il),
            $k('What are the tick boxes in the installer?', 'installer options, tasks installer, desktop shortcut option, start with windows option installer, installer tick boxes', 'Two optional tasks: a desktop shortcut, and Start with Windows (recommended, because the service must be running to receive reports). The last page can also start the service and open the one-time InterLink sign-in.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I update the service to a newer version?', 'update service, upgrade service, newer version service, install over old, update interlink service', 'Run the new setup over the old installation, in the same folder. Your settings (appsettings.Local.json) and the data folder with the InterLink sign-in are kept. Close the program first or let the installer close it.', [], $il),
            $k('Does updating lose my settings or my InterLink sign-in?', 'update loses settings, keep settings update, sign in kept update, update keeps session, lose signin update', 'No. The installer does not contain appsettings.Local.json or the data folder, so an update leaves your address, key and saved InterLink sign-in untouched.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I uninstall the service?', 'uninstall service, remove service, delete service program, remove interlink service, uninstall nexus', 'Windows Settings > Apps > Nexus-L InterLink Service > Uninstall (or Start menu > the uninstall entry). It stops the program, removes the files and the Start-with-Windows entry. The data folder, including the saved InterLink sign-in, is removed too.', [], $il),
            $k('Where do I get the installer?', 'get the installer, installer file, download installer, setup exe location, installer location', 'The setup file is NexusInterlinkService-Setup-1.1.0.exe, kept with the Material Test files on the service computer\'s desktop folder. An administrator can rebuild it from the service source (installer folder).', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I move the service to another computer?', 'move service to another pc, transfer service, new service computer, reinstall other pc, migrate service', 'Install it on the new computer, set the IP, port and key in its Settings, sign in to InterLink there once, then change the service address in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service. Close the old one.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The installer says Windows protected my PC', 'windows protected your pc, smartscreen installer, unknown publisher, blocked installer, run anyway', 'The installer is not signed with a purchased certificate, so SmartScreen warns. Press More info > Run anyway if the file came from your administrator.', [], $il),
            $k('Antivirus blocks the installer or the service', 'antivirus blocks, defender blocks service, quarantine installer, antivirus exe, blocked by security software', 'Ask your administrator to allow the installer and the install folder in the antivirus. The program drives a browser and listens on a port, which some security software treats cautiously.', [], $il),
            $k('Do I need to install .NET for the service?', 'dotnet needed, install .net, net 9 runtime, framework needed, runtime required service', 'No. The installed program is self-contained and already carries what it needs.', [], $il),
            $k('Do I need Chrome or Edge for the service?', 'chrome needed service, edge needed service, browser needed service, which browser service, chromium service', 'Yes, Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge must be installed on the service computer. The service drives it with its own clean profile. Without either, the setup folder offers Install-Browser to download Chromium once.', [], $il),
            $k('First setup after installing', 'first setup service, after install setup, first time service, configure service first, set up the service', 'Open the tray icon > Settings. Set the IP and port, check the NEXUS-L address, press Save and restart, copy the two lines or the key into NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service, then Sign in to InterLink once and press Check.', ['Tray icon > Settings.', 'Set IP / Port, NEXUS-L address; New key if empty.', 'Save and restart.', 'Put the service address and key in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service.', 'Sign in to InterLink... once.', 'Press Check: it must say the service runs and the sign-in is saved.'], $il + $adm),
            $k('Do I need to change the NEXUS-L .env for the service?', 'env service lines, interlinkservice.url env, interlinkservice.key env, env file service, edit env service', 'Not any more when the Admin Settings page is used: the service address and key are saved in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service. The two .env lines (interlinkService.url and interlinkService.key) still work as a fallback.', [], $il + $adm + $goSt),
            $k('The setup finished but nothing appears', 'setup finished nothing appears, no window after install, where is the service after install, tray icon missing after install', 'The service lives in the tray: look for its icon next to the clock (press the up arrow if it is hidden). If it is not there, start it from the Start menu entry Nexus-L InterLink Service.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I start the service manually?', 'start service manually, run service, launch service, start menu service, open the service', 'Start menu > Nexus-L InterLink Service, or the desktop shortcut, or NexusInterlinkService.exe in the install folder.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I stop the service?', 'stop service, exit service, close service, quit tray program, shut service', 'Right-click the tray icon > Exit. Reports sent while it is closed fail with "service not reachable" until it is started again.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I make the service start with Windows?', 'start with windows, autostart service, run at login, startup service, start automatically', 'Tick "Start with Windows" in the service Settings (or in the installer). It then starts when this Windows user logs in. If you ticked it in an older installation, tick it again after moving the program so it points to the new folder.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can the service run without a logged-in user?', 'service without login, run as windows service, scheduled task service, no user logged, headless service run', 'Yes: run NexusInterlinkService.exe with --service from a scheduled task or create a Windows service for it. The one-time InterLink sign-in still has to be done in a visible window by a user first.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The service does not start and shows an error', 'service will not start, error on open, service crashes at start, 0xc000007b, application failed to start', 'Run it from the installed folder (not from a damaged or old copy). If a message like 0xc000007b appears, reinstall with the current setup: the file was probably damaged by the disk. If it still fails, copy the last lines of data\\service.log to the administrator.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The program files look corrupted', 'corrupted service files, damaged service, files corrupt, broken exe, service file damaged', 'Run the installer again over the same folder: it replaces every program file and keeps your settings and data. Do not run the service from a disk that reports errors.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Which port does the service use?', 'service port, which port, port number service, 5077, listening port', 'The port you set in the service Settings (the example in NEXUS-L Settings is port 5077). NEXUS-L must be told the same IP and port, and the firewall must allow it from the NEXUS-L server.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I open the port in the Windows firewall?', 'open firewall port, firewall service, allow inbound port, windows firewall interlink service, firewall rule', 'On the service computer add an inbound rule for TCP on the service port, allowing the NEXUS-L server. An administrator can do it in Windows Defender Firewall > Advanced settings > Inbound Rules > New Rule.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What IP should I choose in the service Settings?', 'which ip service, 0.0.0.0 service, ip address choose, listen address, bind address service', '0.0.0.0 means every address of the service computer and is the simplest. Or pick the one IP that NEXUS-L uses to reach it (for example the 192.168.x.x address).', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can the service computer have a changing IP?', 'dynamic ip service, ip changes service, dhcp service, address changed service, static ip service', 'Give the service computer a fixed (reserved) IP. If the IP changes, update the service address in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service, or sending will fail with "service not reachable".', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Is the installer the same as the published folder?', 'installer vs folder, publish folder, portable folder, copy folder instead, setup or folder', 'The installer carries the same program files compressed, and adds the Start menu entry, optional shortcut, Start with Windows and an uninstaller. A copied folder also runs, but has none of that.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I rebuild the installer?', 'rebuild installer, build setup, make installer, inno setup, create installer exe', 'Publish the service self-contained (dotnet publish -c Release -r win-x64 --self-contained true), then compile installer\\NexusInterlinkService.iss with Inno Setup, passing the publish folder as SourceDir. The result is installer\\output\\NexusInterlinkService-Setup-<version>.exe.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Where is the source of the service?', 'service source code, github service repo, nexusinterlinkservice repository, source c#, where is the code', 'In NEXUS-L under tools\\interlink-service and in the private GitHub repository Gieezzzy/NexusInterlinkService (the same code, with the installer script).', [], $il + $adm),

            // =========================================================== Service Settings window (25)
            $k('How do I open the service Settings?', 'open service settings, service properties, service settings window, tray settings, properties of the service', 'Double-click the tray icon, or right-click it and choose Settings...', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What can I change in the service Settings?', 'what in service settings, service settings options, properties list, service settings fields', 'IP / Port that receive NEXUS-L\'s payload, the shared key, the NEXUS-L address for results and approval checks, the invisible browser option, Start with Windows, the job time limit, and the buttons New key, Copy the lines, Check, Sign in to InterLink and Save and restart.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What is the NEXUS-L address in the service Settings?', 'nexus-l address service, nexus base url service, callback address, where results go, nexus url in service', 'The web address of NEXUS-L, for example http://192.168.32.43/NEXUS-L/. The service sends the result and asks the approval check there.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does New key do?', 'new key button, generate key, make new key, create shared key, new shared key', 'It creates a new random shared key of 16+ characters. After Save and restart, the same key must be put in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service, or sending fails with a key error.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does Copy the lines do?', 'copy the lines, copy lines env, copy service lines, copy settings lines', 'It copies the two lines (service address and key) for NEXUS-L\'s .env, so you can paste them if you do not use the Settings page.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does the Check button show?', 'check button service, check service, service check result, test service, check signed in', 'Whether the service runs and answers, how many reports are waiting, its version, and whether the InterLink sign-in is saved.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does Save and restart do?', 'save and restart, apply service settings, restart service settings, save settings service', 'It writes your settings to appsettings.Local.json and restarts the service so they are used. They stay for every later start; nothing has to be entered again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What is the invisible browser option?', 'invisible browser option, headless option, hide browser, headless setting, show browser option', 'Ticked (normal): the InterLink browser is hidden. Unticked: you see it work, which helps to find out why a step fails. Save and restart to apply.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What is the job time limit?', 'job time limit, job timeout, minutes per job, timeout service, how long job', 'The longest a single report may take before the service gives up and reports a timeout. The default is 20 minutes, because a report with many tests opens many reading pages.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('My service settings are lost after restart', 'settings lost restart, settings not saved service, service forgets address, appsettings local missing, reset settings', 'Settings are kept in appsettings.Local.json next to the program. If they disappear, the program is being started from a different folder or that file was removed or damaged. Start the installed copy and set them again once.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I edit appsettings.Local.json by hand?', 'edit appsettings local, json settings file, manual settings, change settings file', 'Yes, it is plain JSON (Urls, Service:ApiKey, Service:Headless, Nexus:BaseUrl). Restart the service afterwards. The Settings window is safer because it writes a valid file.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I change the port?', 'change port service, new port, different port, port in settings, set port', 'Service Settings > Port, Save and restart. Then enter the new service address in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service and open that port in the firewall.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I change the shared key?', 'change shared key, rotate key, new key service, replace key, update key', 'Press New key in the service Settings, Save and restart, then paste the same key in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service. Both must match.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Where does NEXUS-L know the service address from?', 'service address nexus, where address stored, service url stored, nexus service url', 'From Settings > InterLink service in NEXUS-L (the address and key are saved in the database). If those are empty it falls back to the .env lines.', [], $il + $adm + $goSt),
            $k('The Settings window says the key is too short', 'key too short, key 16 characters, invalid key service, key length', 'The shared key needs at least 16 characters. Press New key to create a proper one.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The Settings window says the port is in use', 'port in use, port already used, address already in use, cannot bind port', 'Another program already uses that port. Pick another port, Save and restart, and use the same port in NEXUS-L.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I see which IPs the computer has?', 'list of ips service, choose ip list, computer ip addresses, ip dropdown, select ip', 'The IP box lists 0.0.0.0 and each address of the service computer; pick the one NEXUS-L can reach.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does Sign in to InterLink do in the Settings window?', 'sign in button settings window, sign in to interlink button, interlink signin service button', 'It opens a visible browser window on the service computer so you can sign in to InterLink (Microsoft sign-in with MFA) once. The session is then saved for the invisible browser.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does Settings stop a running job?', 'settings stop job, restart stops job, restart during job, save while sending', 'Save and restart restarts the service. A job that was running is tried once more after the restart; a waiting job keeps its place in the queue. Avoid restarting while a report is being sent.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The Settings window opens behind other windows', 'settings window behind, window hidden settings, cannot see settings, window not visible', 'Use the tray icon again, or Alt + Tab. Only one Settings window opens at a time.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I open the log from the Settings window?', 'open log from settings, settings log button, log file open, view service log', 'Use the tray menu > Open the log, or open data\\service.log in the install folder.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What should I put in the NEXUS-L address if the server has a name?', 'server name address, hostname nexus address, dns nexus url, nexus url name, use hostname', 'You can use the name if the service computer resolves it, but the IP form (http://192.168.32.43/NEXUS-L/) is the most reliable. Keep the trailing /NEXUS-L/.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I know the service Settings were saved?', 'settings saved check, confirm service settings, did it save, verify settings service', 'After Save and restart, open Settings again and press Check: it reads the running service. The values you typed are shown again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can regular users open the service Settings?', 'users settings service, who can change settings service, access settings service, permissions service settings', 'Anyone logged in to the service computer can open the tray icon, so keep that computer for administrators. The shared key protects the service from the network.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does the service Settings window show the version?', 'version in settings window, title version service, version shown, about service', 'Yes, the version appears in the window and in the Check result. Use it when you report a problem.', [], $il + $adm),

            // =========================================================== Queue and messages (30)
            $k('How does the queue work?', 'queue, fifo queue, first in first out, queue order, how queue works, reports waiting line', 'First in, first out. Everybody\'s reports go into one line and are done one at a time in the order they arrived. Each job is saved on disk until it is done, so closing the program or restarting the computer loses nothing and keeps the order.', [], $il),
            $k('What messages do I get when I press Send?', 'messages after send, notifications send, toasts when send, queued started finished, what messages', 'Three, wherever you are in NEXUS-L: queued (with how many reports are ahead), started, and finished. Finished is a toast plus a Synology message with Labreference, ReportNO and "submitted to InterLink", or the reason it was not.', [], $il),
            $k('My report says queued', 'report says queued, queued message, why queued, waiting message, queued position', 'The service is busy with other reports. The message says how many are ahead of yours; yours starts when they finish.', [], $il),
            $k('How long does one report take?', 'how long one report, time per report, sending duration, minutes per report, speed sending', 'It depends on the number of tests, because every test\'s reading page is opened. A report with many tests can take several minutes; the limit per job is 20 minutes by default.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I send the same application twice?', 'send twice, duplicate send, same application again, double click send, send again waiting', 'Not while it is waiting or being submitted: the second request is refused with "already in the queue", whether it was your double-click or a colleague.', [], $il),
            $k('"already in the queue"', 'already in the queue, already waiting, duplicate queue message, application in queue', 'This application is already waiting or being submitted. Wait for its result message instead of sending again.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I cancel a queued report?', 'cancel queued report, remove from queue, stop my report, cancel send, delete job queue', 'Not from NEXUS-L. An administrator can remove it by closing the service and deleting its file from data\\queue; ask them before it starts.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What happens to the queue if the service restarts?', 'queue after restart, restart queue, power cut queue, computer restart jobs, queue persists', 'The jobs are kept on disk. After the restart they continue in the same order. The job that was running is tried once more; if it is stopped a second time it is reported as failed.', [], $il),
            $k('Where can I see who is waiting?', 'who is waiting, see queue, queue list, view queue, waiting list', 'The Activity window of the service (tray menu), or an administrator can open the queue address of the service. NEXUS-L also lists recent jobs in InterLink Sync.', [], $il),
            $k('What do the job states mean?', 'job states, queued running done failed, signin required state, state meanings, job status words', 'queued: waiting for its turn; running: being submitted; done: InterLink kept it; failed: stopped with a reason; signin-required: InterLink asked for a new sign-in.', [], $il),
            $k('Does a failed job block the queue?', 'failed job blocks, stuck queue, queue stopped after fail, next job after failure', 'No. The failure is reported and the next job starts. Only a lost InterLink sign-in makes the following jobs fail until someone signs in again.', [], $il),
            $k('Why did my report wait so long?', 'report waited long, slow queue, long wait, stuck waiting, delayed report', 'Reports ahead of yours took their turn, and large reports take longer. Look at the Activity window; if the first job is not moving for over 20 minutes it will be stopped by the time limit.', [], $il),
            $k('Can an administrator see failed jobs?', 'see failed jobs, failed jobs list, job failures, which failed, history failed', 'Yes, in the Activity window history, the log and data\\history.jsonl on the service computer. NEXUS-L also stores each job in the table tbl_interlink_service_jobs.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What is tbl_interlink_service_jobs?', 'tbl_interlink_service_jobs, jobs table, service jobs table, interlink service jobs database', 'The NEXUS-L table where each job handed to the service is recorded (who sent it, the state and the result). It is created automatically on first use.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How does NEXUS-L know the result of a job?', 'how nexus knows result, callback result, service callback, result return, report back', 'The service calls NEXUS-L back (interlink/service/callback) with the shared key when the job ends. NEXUS-L stores it, shows the toast and sends the Synology message.', [], $il),
            $k('What is the Synology message when it works?', 'synology message submitted, synology success message, chat message after send, labreference reportno submitted', 'It reads: Labreference: <Lab Ref> / ReportNO: <Report No.> / submitted to InterLink.', [], $il),
            $k('Who receives the Synology message?', 'who receives synology, synology recipient, chat receiver, who gets notice, notification recipient', 'The person who pressed Send gets their own messages. The text and the bot prefix come from NEXUS-L Settings > Synology Chat.', [], $il),
            $k('I did not get a Synology message', 'no synology message, missing chat message, synology not received, no chat notice, synology silent', 'Check that your Synology Chat user is linked in NEXUS-L and that Settings > Synology Chat has the address and bot token. The toast in NEXUS-L shows the same result in any case.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The toast disappeared before I read it', 'toast disappeared, missed the toast, toast too fast, read result again, see result later', 'The result is also in the Synology message and in the job history, so it is not lost. Open InterLink Sync to see recent jobs.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the toast show if I am on another page?', 'toast on other page, notification other page, result any page, toast anywhere', 'Yes. The messages follow you wherever you are in NEXUS-L, as long as a NEXUS-L tab is open.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I close NEXUS-L after pressing Send?', 'close nexus after send, close browser after send, leave page after send, log out after send', 'Yes. The service works on its own. You will still get the Synology message; the toast only shows while a NEXUS-L tab is open.', [], $il),
            $k('What if two colleagues send different reports at once?', 'two colleagues different reports, different reports same time, mixed reports queue, shared account order', 'Both are queued in arrival order and done one after the other, each with its own messages, all in the shared InterLink account.', [], $il),
            $k('Is the order really first in, first out?', 'is queue fifo, order guaranteed, fifo order, arrival order', 'Yes. The service keeps arrival order, also across restarts, because each job is saved as a file when it arrives.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the number of reports ahead mean?', 'reports ahead, how many ahead, ahead of me, position in queue, number ahead', 'How many jobs will be done before yours, including the one running now.', [], $il),
            $k('Is there a limit to the queue length?', 'queue limit, max jobs, maximum queue, queue full, too many jobs', 'There is no fixed limit, but every job takes minutes, so a long queue means a long wait. Send reports as they are approved.', [], $il),
            $k('What happens if NEXUS-L is down when the job ends?', 'nexus down when finish, callback failed, nexus unreachable callback, result not delivered', 'The report is still submitted to InterLink. The result cannot be delivered, so no toast arrives; the service log says the callback failed. Check the application in InterLink and tell an administrator.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does the service resend the callback?', 'callback retry, resend result, retry callback, result retry', 'It tries to deliver the result and logs a failure. If NEXUS-L stayed unreachable, check the report in InterLink and in the job table; an administrator can mark it.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What does "signin-required" mean?', 'signin-required, sign in required, signin required job, need sign in again job', 'InterLink asked for a new sign-in, so the job could not continue. Sign in again from the service computer (Settings > Sign in to InterLink) and send the report again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I see a picture of what InterLink showed?', 'picture of interlink page, see screenshot job, screenshot failure, what interlink showed, shot after save', 'On the service computer open data\\shots: there is a picture after Save and a picture of the page where a job stopped. An administrator can send you the right one.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How are old jobs cleaned up?', 'old jobs cleanup, history cleanup, clean data folder, delete old pictures, history grows', 'Finished jobs leave the queue folder. Only the last 40 pictures are kept. The history and log files grow slowly and can be archived by an administrator.', [], $il + $adm),

            // =========================================================== InterLink sign-in for the service (20)
            $k('How do I sign in the service to InterLink?', 'sign in service interlink, service login, signin service, sign in to interlink service, interlink microsoft sign in service', 'On the service computer: tray icon > Sign in to InterLink... A visible browser opens; sign in with the shared service account (Microsoft sign-in, including MFA). When the InterLink page appears the window closes and the session is saved.', ['Tray icon > Sign in to InterLink...', 'Sign in with the shared account and finish MFA.', 'Wait until the window closes by itself.', 'Press Check in Settings: signed in must be yes.'], $il + $adm),
            $k('Why does the service need a visible sign-in?', 'why visible signin, mfa invisible browser, cannot sign in invisible, microsoft signin invisible, one time visible', 'InterLink uses Microsoft sign-in with MFA, which an invisible browser cannot pass. So it is done once in a visible window and the session is saved for the invisible one.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Is the InterLink password stored by the service?', 'service stores password, password saved service, interlink password service, credentials service stored', 'No password is stored. Only the signed-in session (cookies) is saved in data\\interlink-session.json and refreshed after every job. Protect that file like a password.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How often must I sign in again?', 'how often sign in again, signin expires service, session lifetime, resign in service, repeated sign in', 'Normally not often: the session is refreshed after every job. If InterLink ends it (for example after a long idle time or a password change) jobs fail with "sign in again" and you repeat the sign-in once.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Jobs fail with "sign in again"', 'jobs fail sign in again, sign in again error, interlink asked login, session ended service, relogin service', 'The saved session is no longer valid. Sign in again on the service computer (tray > Sign in to InterLink...), press Check, then send the reports again. The submitter was told on Synology.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The sign-in window closes immediately', 'signin window closes, sign in window closes at once, window disappears signin, signin closes quickly', 'Close any copy of the service\'s browser that is still open and try again. Make sure Chrome or Edge is installed. If it still closes, send the last lines of data\\service.log to an administrator.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The sign-in window does not open', 'signin window does not open, no browser window signin, sign in does nothing, signin button nothing', 'Check that Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge is installed on the service computer and that the program runs under a logged-in user (not as a hidden service). Start the sign-in from the tray menu again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I sign in using --signin?', 'signin command line, --signin, sign in cmd, sign-in-to-interlink cmd, command line signin', 'Yes: NexusInterlinkService.exe --signin opens the same one-time visible sign-in. The Sign-in-to-InterLink.cmd file in the folder does it too.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Which account should be used to sign in?', 'which account sign in service, service account choose, shared account which, account for submitting', 'The shared account that is allowed to add and edit reports for the factory in InterLink. Everything the service submits is recorded under that account.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Where is the saved sign-in kept?', 'saved signin location, session file, interlink-session.json, where session saved', 'In data\\interlink-session.json next to the program. Do not copy it to other computers.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('I changed the InterLink password', 'changed interlink password, password change service, new password service, after password change', 'Sign in again on the service computer so the saved session is replaced. No password is stored in the service, so nothing else has to change.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can two computers share one InterLink session?', 'share session two computers, copy session file, same session two pcs, second computer session', 'No. Sign in on each computer separately, and use only one service at a time on the same account, because InterLink may end the older session.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Check says not signed in', 'check not signed in, signed in no, check says no signin, signin saved no, not signed in service', 'No saved InterLink session was found. Use Sign in to InterLink... on the service computer, then Check again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Check says signed in but jobs fail with sign in', 'signed in but fail, session invalid though saved, check yes but fails, saved session expired', 'The file exists but InterLink has already ended that session. Sign in again; the Check button only tells whether a session is saved, the next job proves it is valid.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does Microsoft ask for MFA each time?', 'mfa each time, microsoft mfa repeat, authenticator every job, mfa prompt service', 'Only at the one-time sign-in. The saved session is reused by every job without another prompt, until InterLink ends it.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Is it safe to leave the service signed in?', 'safe signed in, service signin security, leave signed in, security of session', 'It is as safe as the service computer. Keep it in a locked room or account, allow only the NEXUS-L server through the firewall, and keep the shared key secret.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I sign out the service from InterLink?', 'sign out service, remove session, logout service, delete saved session, clear signin', 'Close the service and delete data\\interlink-session.json. The next sign-in then starts fresh.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What if InterLink asks to accept new terms?', 'interlink new terms, accept terms, interlink consent, terms popup, new policy interlink', 'A person must accept the terms once in a visible sign-in (Sign in to InterLink...). The invisible browser cannot decide that for you.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What if InterLink shows a captcha or a verification?', 'interlink captcha, verification page, human check interlink, extra verification', 'Complete it in the visible sign-in window. The service never bypasses captchas or verifications; it only reuses the session you finished.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I use my own account to sign the service in?', 'my own account service, personal account service, use my login, sign in with my account', 'It works technically, but then every submitted report is recorded under your name. Use the shared service account agreed by the lab.', [], $il + $adm),

            // =========================================================== Troubleshooting (45)
            $k('"service_unreachable"', 'service_unreachable, service not reachable, service did not answer, background service did not answer, cannot reach service', 'NEXUS-L could not reach the service. Check that the tray program is running, that the address in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service has the right IP and port, and that the Windows firewall allows that port from the NEXUS-L server. The browser extension is used instead when it is installed.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The service did not answer: using the browser extension instead', 'using the browser extension instead, fallback to extension, service fallback, extension fallback toast', 'NEXUS-L could not reach the service and switched to the extension. Install and sign in with the extension for that send, and ask an administrator to check the service (running, address, firewall).', [], $il),
            $k('"Wrong service key" or 401', 'wrong service key, 401 service, key rejected, unauthorized service, invalid key', 'The key in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service differs from the key in the service Settings. Copy the same key to both and Save.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Check in NEXUS-L Settings shows the service is down', 'service down settings, settings check service down, service status offline, offline service', 'The "Test the service" button could not reach the address. Verify that the program runs, the IP and port, and the firewall; open http://<ip>:<port>/health in a browser from the NEXUS-L server to test.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I test the service address in a browser?', 'test health address, health endpoint, open health, service health url, ping service', 'Open http://<service-ip>:<port>/health. It needs no key and answers with ok, the number waiting, whether it is signed in and the version.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('A report with the entered report number has already exists', 'report number already exists, duplicate report number interlink, report no already used, already exists interlink, a report with the entered report number', 'InterLink refuses a Report No. that is already used by another application. NEXUS-L checks this before sending; change the Report No. in the report to an unused one and send again, or use Edit mode if this is the same application.', [], $il),
            $k('Why does InterLink refuse a duplicate Report No.?', 'why refuse duplicate report no, report no unique, same report number two applications, duplicate rule', 'InterLink keeps each Report No. unique across applications. The service reads InterLink\'s pop-up message after Save and reports it as the reason.', [], $il),
            $k('The report was saved but has no Report No. in InterLink', 'saved but no report no, report no missing grid, save not kept, proof of save, saved nothing', 'The service does not trust "no error". After Save it searches the grid again and needs the Report No. to appear. If it does not, the job is failed with that reason, so you know it was not kept.', [], $il),
            $k('Only Heat Aging has rows in InterLink', 'only heat aging rows, test element rows missing, only one test uploaded, other tests missing, rows missing interlink', 'InterLink creates the Test Element rows only when a test\'s reading page is opened. Sender 1.7.3 and the service now open the reading page of every test, so all tests get their rows. Update the extension to 1.7.3 or use the service.', [], $il),
            $k('The InterLink rows are empty after sending', 'rows empty after sending, empty test elements, no values uploaded, readings missing interlink', 'Check the report has values in each test, that the report was approved, and that you used sender 1.7.3 or the current service. Send again in Edit mode if the application already exists.', [], $il),
            $k('Test Element for Color Change is not empty', 'color change element, color change test element empty, color change element value', 'For Color Change the Test Element is left empty on purpose. The service and sender 1.7.3 empty it.', [], $il),
            $k('What is put in Test Element for Corrosion?', 'corrosion test element, corrosion elements, specimen joined, specimen 1 specimen 2, corrosion test elements', 'The Test Element equals Specimen 1, Specimen 2 and so on, joined together, as InterLink expects. Heat Aging keeps its existing element rows and only missing ones are added.', [], $il),
            $k('Why are Sample ID, Test Item Name and Test Method not sent for every test?', 'sample id test item name test method not all, values not all tests, fewer values sent, only elements sent', 'Those fields are the same for the whole report and are filled once; per test only what InterLink needs to create its rows is sent.', [], $il),
            $k('A step of the job failed on the Upload Form', 'step failed upload form, form step error, upload form stopped, job stopped upload form, failed at form', 'Open the picture of the page where the job stopped (data\\shots on the service computer) and the log line "InterLink says: ..." to see what InterLink showed. Usually a required box is empty or a list value does not exist.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('InterLink refused a box value (list of values)', 'list of values refused, lov value not found, value not in list, lov popup no match, value does not exist interlink', 'The value from NEXUS-L is not in InterLink\'s list for that box (for example a Test Package or Season). Check Settings > InterLink report defaults against InterLink\'s list and correct the spelling.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The job timed out', 'job timed out, timeout error, job took too long, time limit reached, 20 minutes timeout', 'The job passed the time limit (20 minutes by default). Big reports or a slow InterLink can do this. Send it again; if it repeats, ask an administrator to raise the limit in the service Settings.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('InterLink is slow today', 'interlink slow, slow interlink, pages load slowly, interlink lag', 'The service waits for InterLink\'s pages and then continues, so a slow day means longer jobs and a longer queue, not lost reports. Check the Activity window.', [], $il),
            $k('The service uses a lot of memory', 'service memory, high memory, ram service, browser memory, service heavy', 'The invisible browser needs memory while a job runs. Keep other heavy programs off the service computer and restart the service if it has been running for weeks.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Chrome or Edge was not found by the service', 'chrome not found service, edge not found, browser not found, no browser service, browser launcher error', 'Install Google Chrome or Microsoft Edge on the service computer, or run Install-Browser once to download Chromium, then start the service again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The service says the Scripts file is missing', 'scripts missing, interlink-core.js missing, core script missing, scripts folder missing', 'The Scripts\\interlink-core.js file next to the program is gone or empty. Reinstall with the current setup to restore it.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Settings page says the service key is not set', 'service key not set, key empty settings, no key set, missing key', 'Enter the shared key in NEXUS-L Settings > InterLink service (the same as in the service Settings) and Save.', [], $st + $goSt),
            $k('The report reached InterLink but NEXUS-L shows no result', 'no result shown, interlink has it nexus no result, callback missing, result not shown', 'The callback may not have arrived. Open the application in InterLink to confirm, check the service log for a failed callback, and verify the NEXUS-L address in the service Settings.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I check that a report really got into InterLink?', 'check report in interlink, verify submitted, confirm report in interlink, is it in interlink, proof submitted', 'In InterLink search the application: the row must show a Report No. and the attachment. The service itself already checked the Report No. in the grid before calling the job done.', [], $il),
            $k('NEXUS-L says it is not approved', 'not approved send, approval missing send, send says not approved, approve before send', 'Only a report approved and signed by a Manager or Supervisor is sent. Ask for the approval (the link or QR is sent to them) and send again after it is signed.', [], $il),
            $k('The approval link expired', 'approval link expired, qr expired, link expired, approve link time, expired approval', 'The link works for the number of minutes set in Settings > Report approval (60 by default). Send a new approval request from the report.', [], $il),
            $k('Where is the signed PDF kept?', 'signed pdf location, approvals folder, writable approvals, signed pdf stored, where is signed pdf', 'In NEXUS-L\'s writable/approvals folder as <id>_signed.pdf next to the html. This folder is not published to Git because it contains report data.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The service says the PDF is missing', 'pdf missing service, no pdf in job, job without pdf, attachment missing job', 'The job reached the service without the signed PDF. Make sure the report is approved and signed, then press Send again so NEXUS-L rebuilds the job.', [], $il),
            $k('The InterLink grid does not show my application', 'grid does not show application, application not found grid, search application not found, cannot find application', 'The service searches by Application No. If it is not found, check the number for typing mistakes and that the application exists in InterLink for the signed-in account.', [], $il),
            $k('Which mode does the service use, Add or Edit?', 'add or edit mode, mode add edit service, which mode, add edit decide, add mode edit mode', 'Add when the application has no report in InterLink yet, Edit when it already has one (the popup menu on the Upload Form offers Add and Edit). NEXUS-L sends the mode it needs with the job.', [], $il),
            $k('What is Edit mode for?', 'edit mode purpose, why edit mode, update existing report, resend corrected report, correct a sent report', 'To correct a report that is already in InterLink: the service opens the existing Upload Form in Edit and replaces the values and the PDF, instead of adding a second report.', [], $il),
            $k('Edit mode refused my change', 'edit mode refused, edit not allowed, cannot edit interlink, edit locked, locked report interlink', 'InterLink may lock a report after review or approval on its side. Check the status in InterLink; only a report still editable can be corrected by the service.', [], $il),
            $k('The service posted values but the status stays pending', 'status pending after send, pending status interlink, status not changed, interlink status', 'The service submits the Upload Form; what InterLink does with the status afterwards is InterLink\'s own review process.', [], $il),
            $k('I see "A005..." application numbers in the messages', 'application number format, a005 number, what is a005, application no format', 'That is the InterLink Application No. of the report (for example A005986061). The message pairs it with the NEXUS-L Lab Reference and the Report No.', [], $il),
            $k('Why did the job say the report number is used by another application?', 'report number used by another application, nexus refuses early report no used, early refusal report no, report no taken', 'NEXUS-L looks up the Report No. before building the job and refuses early if another application already has it, so you do not wait in the queue for a certain failure.', [], $il),
            $k('Do pop-up messages from InterLink get lost?', 'interlink popup messages lost, alert read, dialog messages read, message boxes interlink, toast interlink read', 'No. The service reads InterLink\'s alert, confirm and toast messages, writes them to the log as "InterLink says: ..." and uses them as the reason when a job fails.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Where do I find the reason a job failed?', 'reason job failed, why job failed, failure reason, find failure, job error reason', 'In the Synology message and toast sent to you, in the Activity window history, and in the log line near the end of that job in data\\service.log.', [], $il),
            $k('The service log is empty', 'log empty, no log lines, service log missing, empty service log', 'The program was not started from its installed folder, or the data folder cannot be written. Start it from the installed shortcut and check the folder permissions.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The Activity window is empty', 'activity empty, nothing in activity, activity window blank, no jobs shown', 'Nothing is waiting or running, or the history is not loaded yet. Press the refresh button or reopen the window after sending a report.', [], $il),
            $k('A job is stuck in running', 'job stuck running, running forever, stuck job, job not finishing, hanging job', 'The time limit (20 minutes by default) ends it as failed. If the browser is truly hanging, exit and start the service: the job is tried once more, and failed if it stops again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What if the service computer was shut down during a job?', 'shutdown during job, power off during job, pc off mid job, interrupted job', 'On the next start the job is retried once. If it was already saved in InterLink, the Report No. check finds it; otherwise it is submitted again. A second interruption reports it as failed.', [], $il),
            $k('Could a report be added twice to InterLink?', 'report twice interlink, duplicate in interlink, double submission, added twice', 'The queue refuses an application that is already waiting, and InterLink refuses a duplicate Report No., so a second copy is stopped.', [], $il),
            $k('What do I do first when sending fails?', 'sending fails what first, first steps failure, troubleshoot sending, send problem checklist', 'Read the reason in the toast or Synology message. If it mentions the service, check the tray program and address; if it mentions sign in, sign the service in again; if it mentions a value, fix the report or the Settings default and send again.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I report a service problem to the administrator?', 'report service problem, contact admin service, what to send admin, log to send, give information problem', 'Give the Application No., the Lab Reference, the time, the message you got and the last 30 lines of data\\service.log with the picture from data\\shots if there is one.', [], $il),

            // =========================================================== Settings page (60)
            $k('Where is the Settings page?', 'settings page, where settings, open settings nexus, admin settings, system settings, find settings', 'In the sidebar: Settings. It is visible and usable only for users whose role is Admin.', [], $goSt),
            $k('Who can open the Settings page?', 'who can open settings, settings access, admin only settings, settings permission, role admin settings', 'Only users with the role Admin (Role column in the user access list). Other users do not see the item and the page refuses them.', [], $goSt),
            $k('What is in the Settings page?', 'settings page contents, what settings contains, settings sections, settings categories', 'InterLink service (address, key, on/off), Database in use (test and switch), Transfer to another database, InterLink report defaults, Report approval (link time) and Synology Chat (address, bot token, prefix).', [], $goSt),
            $k('Where are the settings saved?', 'where settings saved, settings table, tbl_system_settings, settings database, saved settings location', 'In the table tbl_system_settings (created automatically). An empty value falls back to the .env file where it makes sense, for example for Synology.', [], $adm),
            $k('Do settings apply right away?', 'settings apply immediately, settings need restart, effect of settings, save and use, instant settings', 'Yes for NEXUS-L itself: the next page or send uses the new value. The service program has its own settings, which need Save and restart there.', [], $st),
            $k('What does "Send reports through the background service" do?', 'send reports through background service, service enabled setting, service on off setting, use service toggle', 'On: Send uses the C# service. Off: the browser extension does the sending instead. Turn it off when the service is being maintained.', [], $st),
            $k('What do I enter as the Service address?', 'service address setting, service url setting, ip and port setting, address of service nexus', 'The IP and port set in the service program, written as http://<ip>:<port>, for example http://192.168.32.43:5077.', [], $st),
            $k('What is the Shared key setting?', 'shared key setting, key setting password, service key field, key box', 'The same secret as in the service Settings. It is a password field: after saving it is never shown again; type a new one only to change it.', [], $st),
            $k('Why is the key box empty after saving?', 'key box empty after save, password field empty, key not shown, hidden key', 'Password fields are never shown again for safety. Empty with a saved value means it is stored; leave it empty to keep the stored key.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I test the service from the Settings page?', 'test service settings page, check service button, test connection service, check connection service', 'Use the "Test the service" button in the InterLink service section: it asks the service for its health and shows whether it runs, how many reports wait and whether it is signed in.', [], $st),
            $k('What are the InterLink report defaults?', 'interlink report defaults, report defaults settings, default values interlink, default boxes interlink', 'The values a new InterLink report starts with: Service Provider, Lab Location, Service Test Type, Test Stage, Service Required, email recipients, company, Interlink Code, vendor and factory details, brand, season, sourcing office, export, origin, category, test packages and factory address.', [], $st),
            $k('Do the report defaults reach the forms?', 'defaults reach forms, defaults used where, settings reflected views, defaults applied upload form, defaults manage reports', 'Yes. They fill the Upload Form, the Manage Reports form, new report rows, and the values sent to InterLink by the service and the extension.', [], $st),
            $k('I changed a default but the Upload Form shows the old value', 'default old value upload form, settings not reflected, old default shown, change not visible', 'Reload the page (Ctrl + F5). Defaults fill new reports; an already saved report keeps its own values until you change them.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the Season?', 'change season setting, season default, set season, season s27', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Season. Use the spelling that exists in InterLink\'s list.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the Test Package?', 'change test package setting, test packages default, package default, vans pull strength setting', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Test Package(s). It must match a package in InterLink.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the email recipients?', 'email recipients setting, notification email default, change recipients, email notification recipient', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Email Notification Recipient(s). Separate several addresses as InterLink expects.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the factory details?', 'factory details setting, factory name id address, change factory, factory city country province', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults: Factory Name, Factory ID, Factory Address, Country, City and State / Province.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the vendor?', 'vendor setting, vendor name id, change vendor, vendor default', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults: Vendor Name and Vendor ID.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the brand?', 'brand setting, buyer brand setting, change brand, brand name default', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Brand Name.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the Interlink Code?', 'interlink code setting, change interlink code, code default, company code', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Interlink Code (with the Company Name beside it).', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the Lab Location?', 'lab location setting, change lab location, location default, philippines lab', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Lab Location.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the Service Test Type?', 'service test type setting, in-house testing setting, test type default', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Service Test Type (and Test Stage and Service Required beside it).', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the country of origin?', 'country of origin setting, origin default, product export to, product category setting', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults: Country of Origin, Product Export To and Product Category.', [], $st),
            $k('Which setting changes the Sourcing Office?', 'sourcing office setting, change sourcing office, aso default', 'Settings > InterLink report defaults > Sourcing Office.', [], $st),
            $k('Can I go back to the default value of a setting?', 'reset setting default, restore default value, revert setting, default value button', 'Clear the box and save: an empty value uses the built-in default shown as the placeholder (and the .env value where one exists).', [], $st),
            $k('What does the Report approval setting do?', 'report approval setting, approval link minutes, approval link works for, link expiry setting', 'Settings > Report approval > Approval link works for (minutes). The QR / link sent to the Manager or Supervisor expires after this time (60 by default).', [], $st),
            $k('How do I make the approval link last longer?', 'approval link longer, extend approval link, increase approval minutes, link lasts', 'Raise the number of minutes in Settings > Report approval and save. It applies to the next approval request.', [], $st),
            $k('What do the Synology settings do?', 'synology settings, synology address bot token prefix, chat settings, bot prefix setting', 'Settings > Synology Chat holds the Synology Chat address, the bot token (password field) and an optional message prefix put before every message the bot sends. Empty address or token uses the .env values.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I change the Synology bot token?', 'change bot token, new synology token, update token, synology token setting', 'Settings > Synology Chat > Bot token: type the new token and save. The old one is replaced and never shown again.', [], $st),
            $k('What is the message prefix?', 'message prefix, bot prefix, prefix synology, text before message', 'A short text put before every message the bot sends, for example a tag showing the message comes from NEXUS-L. Empty means none.', [], $st),
            $k('What does the Database in use section show?', 'database in use, which database, current database, db in use settings, database section', 'The database NEXUS-L uses right now: server, port, database name and user. You can test another set of values and switch to it.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I test a database connection?', 'test database connection, db test button, check database connection, test db settings', 'Fill server, port, database, user and password in Database in use and press Test this connection. It tries to connect and tells you whether it worked, without changing anything.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I switch NEXUS-L to another database?', 'switch database, change database, use other database, db switch confirm, switch to another db', 'Enter the new values, press Test this connection, then type SWITCH in the confirm box and press Use this database. NEXUS-L writes the new connection into the .env file and uses it from the next request.', ['Fill the connection values.', 'Press Test this connection and wait for success.', 'Type SWITCH in the confirm box.', 'Press Use this database.'], $st),
            $k('Why do I have to type SWITCH?', 'type switch confirm, why switch word, confirm switch database, switch safety', 'Switching the database changes where all data is read and written. The confirm word stops an accidental click.', [], $st),
            $k('Is switching the database reversible?', 'switch database reversible, undo database switch, go back database, revert db switch', 'Yes: switch again to the previous values. The old database is not changed or deleted by switching; only the connection moves.', [], $st),
            $k('Where does the switch write the new database?', 'switch writes where, env database change, which file db settings, .env database values', 'Into the .env file (database.default.*). Keep a copy of .env before switching.', [], $adm),
            $k('Which database is the test database?', 'test database, which is the test db, test database name, dbnexus test, test environment database', 'Use Test this connection in Database in use to try values. The system runs on the database named under Database in use; use the Transfer section to copy the data to a test or backup database.', [], $st),
            $k('What does Transfer to another database do?', 'transfer database, copy database, transfer to another database, move data to another db, database transfer', 'It copies all NEXUS-L tables and data to another MySQL server or database that you specify (server, port, database, user, password). The current database is only read.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I transfer the data to another database?', 'how transfer data database, steps transfer database, copy data to new database, run transfer', 'Enter the target connection, tick Create the database if it does not exist when needed, tick Overwrite only if the target tables may be emptied, and press Start the transfer. A summary shows each table and its row count.', ['Enter the target server, port, database, user and password.', 'Tick Create the database if it does not exist (if needed).', 'Tick Overwrite only when the target tables may be emptied first.', 'Press Start the transfer and read the table summary.'], $st),
            $k('What does "Overwrite tables that already have rows" mean?', 'overwrite tables rows, overwrite option transfer, empty target tables, overwrite target', 'If a target table already holds rows, it is emptied first and then filled from the current database. Without the tick, such tables are skipped so nothing is lost.', [], $st),
            $k('What does "Create the database if it does not exist" do?', 'create database option, create target database, new database transfer, create if not exist', 'If the target database name does not exist on the target server, it is created first, so the transfer can fill it.', [], $st),
            $k('Is the transfer safe for my current data?', 'transfer safe, transfer harm data, does transfer delete, transfer risk current db', 'The current database is only read. Only the target can be changed, and only when you tick Overwrite.', [], $st),
            $k('How long does the transfer take?', 'transfer duration, how long database transfer, transfer speed, transfer slow', 'It depends on the data size and the network. Do not close the page until the table summary appears.', [], $st),
            $k('Can I run the transfer from the command line?', 'transfer command line, spark settings transfer, cli transfer, php spark transfer', 'Yes. An administrator can run php spark settings:transfer on the server; it does the same copy as the Settings page.', [], $adm),
            $k('The transfer says access denied', 'transfer access denied, mysql access denied, target user rights, grant privileges transfer', 'The target user cannot connect from the NEXUS-L server or lacks rights. Ask the database administrator to grant create, insert and drop on that database to the user.', [], $st),
            $k('Test connection fails with "unknown host"', 'unknown host database, cannot resolve server, host not found db, db server name fails', 'The server name or IP is wrong or not reachable from the NEXUS-L server. Use the IP address and check the network.', [], $st),
            $k('Can I switch back to the main database after testing?', 'switch back main database, return to main db, go back after test, restore connection', 'Yes. Enter the main database values, Test this connection, then Use this database. Write down the main values before switching.', [], $st),
            $k('Is the Settings page logged?', 'settings changes logged, who changed settings, audit settings, updated_by settings', 'Each saved setting stores who changed it and when (updated_by and updated_at in the table).', [], $adm),
            $k('Can I export my settings?', 'export settings, backup settings, copy settings, settings backup', 'Use the Transfer section to copy the tables, including tbl_system_settings, to a backup database.', [], $st),
            $k('A non-admin sees "access denied" on Settings', 'access denied settings, forbidden settings, not allowed settings page, settings 403', 'Only users with the role Admin may open Settings. Ask an administrator to change your Role in the user access list.', [], $goSt),
            $k('How do I make someone an Admin?', 'make admin, give admin role, set role admin, change user role, user access role', 'In the user access list set the Role of that user to Admin. They see Settings after their next page load.', [], $adm),
            $k('Settings shows a toast Saved', 'settings saved toast, saved message settings, settings save confirmation', 'The change is stored and used right away. If it says it failed, the message gives the reason, for example an invalid address.', [], $st),
            $k('Settings page keeps asking me to log in', 'settings login again, settings redirects login, session settings page, settings logged out', 'Your NEXUS-L session ended. Log in again; the Settings page opens afterwards if your role is Admin.', [], $goSt),
            $k('Do settings differ per user?', 'settings per user, personal settings, user specific settings, global settings', 'No. Settings are global for the whole system. Personal preferences, such as theme, are separate.', [], $st),
            $k('Can I hide the key from other admins?', 'hide key admins, key visibility, who sees key, secret visibility', 'The key and tokens are password fields and are never shown again after saving, to any admin.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I check what the service address is without showing the key?', 'view service address, check address only, see saved address, address saved', 'The address box shows the saved address; only the key box stays blank.', [], $st),
            $k('What is the first thing to set up in Settings?', 'first setting to set, initial settings, setup settings order, what to configure first', 'InterLink service: the address and key of the service, then press Check. After that review the report defaults, the approval link time and the Synology details.', [], $st),
            $k('Does the Settings page change the .env for everything?', 'settings change env, env vs settings, settings or env, which wins env settings', 'No. Only the database switch writes .env. Other settings live in the database and, if empty, fall back to the .env values.', [], $adm),
            $k('What if Settings and .env disagree?', 'settings and env disagree, settings override env, conflict settings env, which value used', 'A non-empty value in Settings is used. Leave it empty to use the .env value.', [], $adm),
            $k('Can I use Settings on my phone?', 'settings on phone, mobile settings, settings small screen, tablet settings', 'Yes, the page adapts to small screens, but a computer is easier for the database transfer.', [], $st),

            // =========================================================== Approval and sending flow (30)
            $k('What are the steps from report to InterLink?', 'steps report to interlink, whole process, report workflow interlink, from report to submitted, end to end', 'Make and save the report in QC Lab Reports, request the approval, a Manager or Supervisor approves and signs it, then press Send to InterLink. The service submits it and you get the result.', ['Save the report.', 'Request approval (link or QR to the Manager / Supervisor).', 'They approve and sign; the signed PDF is made.', 'Press Send to InterLink.', 'Read the toast or Synology message.'], $il),
            $k('Who can approve a report?', 'who can approve, approver role, manager supervisor approve, approval who', 'A Manager or Supervisor, using the link or QR code sent to them. They review the report and sign.', [], $il),
            $k('How does a Manager approve from the phone?', 'approve from phone, approval qr scan, approval link phone, mobile approval', 'They open the link or scan the QR, review the report page, sign on screen and confirm. The signed PDF is created and the report becomes sendable.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the signed PDF contain?', 'signed pdf contains, signature on report, signed report content, signature image pdf', 'The report sheet as approved with the approver\'s signature, saved as <id>_signed.pdf. That is the file attached in InterLink.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I send a report that was changed after approval?', 'change after approval, edit after approved, modified after approval, resend after change', 'No: a change needs a new approval, because the signed PDF no longer matches. Request the approval again and send after it is signed.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I send many reports at once?', 'send many reports, bulk send, send several, multiple reports send, send batch', 'Send each approved report; they go into the queue and run in order. Each has its own messages.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the Send button check first?', 'send button checks, checks before send, validation before send, what is checked', 'The report is approved and signed, the Application No. and Lab Reference exist, the Report No. is not used by another application, and the service (or extension) is available.', [], $il),
            $k('Which Report No. is used?', 'which report no, report number source, report number format, where report no comes', 'The Report No. of the report in NEXUS-L (Manage Reports). Make sure it is unique in InterLink; NEXUS-L warns when another application already has it.', [], $il),
            $k('Where do I set the Report No.?', 'set report no, edit report number, report no field, manage reports report no', 'In Manage Reports / the report form of the application, in the Report No. box, before sending.', [], $il),
            $k('What is the Pre-Sync dialog?', 'pre-sync dialog, presync, pre sync window, before sync dialog', 'The window that asks which Lab Reference belongs to the application and shows the values that will be sent, so you can check them before sending.', [], $il),
            $k('What does Add vs Edit mean for me?', 'add vs edit me, add edit user, choose add edit, what is add mode', 'Add creates the report in InterLink for the first time; Edit corrects a report already there. NEXUS-L picks the mode from the application; you only press Send.', [], $il),
            $k('How do I correct a report that is already in InterLink?', 'correct sent report, fix submitted report, change report in interlink, resubmit corrected', 'Correct it in NEXUS-L, request approval again, and Send: the service uses Edit mode and replaces the values and the PDF in the existing InterLink report.', [], $il),
            $k('Does Edit mode create a second report?', 'edit creates second report, duplicate on edit, edit new report, edit duplicates', 'No. Edit opens the existing Upload Form of the same application and changes it.', [], $il),
            $k('Which tests are sent for a report?', 'which tests sent, tests included, every test sent, tests in report sent, all tests upload', 'Every test in the report: the reading page of each test is opened in InterLink so its Test Element rows exist, and the values are filled.', [], $il),
            $k('Why are the reading pages opened?', 'why reading pages opened, reading page purpose, update and go back, test element rows created', 'InterLink creates the Test Element rows of a test only when its reading page is opened. The service opens each one, fills it and uses Update and Go Back.', [], $il),
            $k('What is the Test Element column?', 'test element column, what is test element, element names, test elements meaning', 'The row name in InterLink\'s reading table (for example Specimen 1, Specimen 2 or a material part). NEXUS-L maps each test\'s labels to InterLink\'s names.', [], $il),
            $k('What is put in Test Element for Heat Aging?', 'heat aging test element, heat aging rows, heat aging elements, keep heat aging rows', 'The rows that already exist in InterLink for Heat Aging are kept; only the missing ones are added. Nothing is removed.', [], $il),
            $k('Are measurements converted before sending?', 'measurements converted, units converted send, value conversion, converted values interlink', 'Values are sent as saved in the report, with the unit InterLink expects for that test. Check the report preview if a value looks different.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the report PDF show all tests?', 'pdf shows all tests, all tests in pdf, pdf complete, pdf pages tests', 'Yes, the signed PDF is the report sheet as approved. Check it in the preview before requesting the approval.', [], $il),
            $k('What happens if a required InterLink box has no default?', 'required box no default, missing default box, empty required box, default missing interlink', 'The service reports which box was empty or refused. Set the default in Settings > InterLink report defaults or fill the value in the report, then send again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I send a report for another factory?', 'another factory report, different factory send, factory change send, other factory defaults', 'The factory fields come from the report defaults in Settings. For another factory, an administrator changes the defaults first, or the report carries its own values if they differ.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does sending change my NEXUS-L report?', 'sending changes report, send modifies report, report changed after send, status after send', 'It records the send result (Report No. in InterLink, state and time) but does not change the test values.', [], $il),
            $k('Where can I see the send history of a report?', 'send history report, see past sends, history of sends, previous submissions', 'In InterLink Sync, the recent jobs list, and in the job table. The Synology messages are also a record.', [], $il),
            $k('What is the Report Detail page?', 'report detail page, report detail, detail of report, report details view, detail view', 'The page that shows a report completely: header details, every test with its readings, the approval and InterLink state. It was widened and completed so nothing is cut.', [], []),
            $k('How do I open the Report Detail page?', 'open report detail, view report detail, report detail open, go to detail', 'From the report list click the report (or its detail button). The page opens with all sections.', [], []),
            $k('The Report Detail table is cut at the edge', 'detail table cut, table cut off, table width detail, scroll detail table, table too wide', 'The page now uses the full width and scrolls the table sideways when needed. Reload with Ctrl + F5 if you still see the old layout.', [], []),
            $k('Why can I not scroll the background behind a dialog?', 'background scroll dialog, cannot scroll behind, dialog scroll lock, scroll locked popup', 'While a dialog is open the background is locked on purpose, so you scroll the dialog content only. Close the dialog to scroll the page again.', [], []),
            $k('Which InterLink fields come from the report?', 'fields from the report, which fields report to interlink, field mapping, map report fields', 'The application, report number, lab reference, tests with their readings and the signed PDF come from the report; the factory and vendor style values come from Settings > InterLink report defaults.', [], $il),
            $k('Can the extension still be used?', 'extension still used, sender still works, use extension anyway, extension available', 'Yes: with Send Service off in Settings, or when the service is unreachable, the NEXUS-L InterLink Sender extension (1.7.3 or newer) does the sending in your own Chrome.', [], $il),
            $k('Which extension version should I have?', 'extension version, sender version, 1.7.3 sender, update extension, newest sender', 'Version 1.7.3 or newer: it opens the reading page of every test so all tests get rows. Download the current sender from InterLink Sync and Load unpacked again (Chrome or Firefox).', [], $il),
            $k('How do I update the extension?', 'update sender extension, reload extension, new extension zip, update sender, replace extension', 'Download the sender again, unzip it over the old folder, then at chrome://extensions press the reload icon on the sender. Reload the NEXUS-L page.', [], $il),

            // =========================================================== Assistant and misc (about 25)
            $k('What can the assistant tell me about the service?', 'assistant service help, bot service questions, ask about service, what bot knows service', 'How it works, installing and updating it, its Settings, the queue and messages, signing in to InterLink, and what each error means. Ask in your own words, for example "report stuck in queue".', [], []),
            $k('Can the assistant restart the service?', 'bot restart service, assistant restart service, restart service from nexus, control service bot', 'No. The service is controlled on its own computer (tray icon). I can explain the steps and what to check.', [], []),
            $k('Can the assistant see the service queue?', 'bot see queue, assistant queue list, check queue assistant, queue status bot', 'I explain how the queue works. To see who is waiting use the Activity window of the service or the recent jobs in InterLink Sync.', [], []),
            $k('How do I ask about a failed report?', 'ask about failed report, bot failed report help, explain failure assistant, why my report failed bot', 'Type the message you got, for example "A report with the entered report number has already exists" or "sign in again", and I give the cause and the steps.', [], []),
            $k('Which messages does the assistant know?', 'which errors assistant knows, error list bot, messages known, bot error coverage', 'service_unreachable, wrong service key, sign in again, report number already exists, already in the queue, not approved, time out, no PDF, and the InterLink value-list errors.', [], []),
            $k('Is the service available on the mobile app?', 'service mobile app, rms app service, phone service, android service', 'The service is a Windows program. The mobile app only receives NEXUS-L\'s own notifications; sending to InterLink happens on the server side.', [], []),
            $k('What is new in this version of NEXUS-L?', 'whats new, new features, new in nexus, latest changes, new function', 'The InterLink background service with a queue, the Admin Settings page (service, report defaults, approval link time, Synology, database switch and transfer), reading pages of every test, Add / Edit mode, proof of save, the service installer, and a fuller Report Detail page.', [], []),
            $k('What changed for report defaults?', 'report defaults changed, defaults new, defaults moved settings, defaults not fixed', 'They are no longer fixed in the code. They live in Settings > InterLink report defaults and reach every form and the values sent to InterLink.', [], $st),
            $k('What changed about Synology messages?', 'synology messages changed, new synology text, chat format changed, message format', 'After a send, the bot writes: Labreference / ReportNO / submitted to InterLink, or the reason it failed, to the person who sent it.', [], []),
            $k('What changed about duplicates?', 'duplicates changed, duplicate rules new, duplicate guard, no duplicate sends', 'The same application cannot be queued twice, and a Report No. used by another application is refused before sending.', [], $il),
            $k('Is there a manual for the service?', 'manual service, documentation service, readme service, guide service, service docs', 'Yes: the README in the service folder (tools\\interlink-service) covers setup, Settings, the queue and the endpoints, and this assistant explains the same in short steps.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What ports and addresses does NEXUS-L use for the service?', 'ports addresses service, endpoints service, health jobs queue endpoint, service api', 'The service listens on its own IP and port. NEXUS-L calls /jobs, /jobs/{id}, /queue and /health there with the shared key (health needs none), and the service calls NEXUS-L\'s callback and verify addresses.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I run NEXUS-L and the service on the same computer?', 'same computer nexus and service, one pc both, nexus server and service together, combined install', 'Yes, as long as the computer has Chrome or Edge, a logged-in user for the tray program and a free port. A separate computer keeps the server clean and is the usual choice.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Where did the project move to?', 'project moved, new folder e drive, e html nexus-l, moved from d drive, site location', 'NEXUS-L now lives in E:\\html\\NEXUS-L (web root E:\\html), after the old D: volume showed errors. The site address is unchanged.', [], $adm),
            $k('Why were some files repaired?', 'files repaired, corrupted files nexus, disk errors repair, damaged files repaired', 'The old D: volume had cross-linked clusters that mixed file contents. Damaged files were restored from Git and checked, and the service program was replaced with a clean copy.', [], $adm),
            $k('How do I check that NEXUS-L files are sound?', 'check files sound, deploy check, health check files, verify installation, php spark deploy:check', 'An administrator runs php spark deploy:check; it reports READY when the requirements, folders and disk are fine.', [], $adm),
            $k('Is the approvals folder in Git?', 'approvals in git, writable approvals git, public repo approvals, report data in git', 'It must not be: it holds report pages and PDFs. Keep writable/ out of the repository.', [], $adm),
            $k('Who do I ask when the service is not working?', 'who to ask service not working, contact for service, administrator service, support service', 'Your NEXUS-L administrator. Give the Application No., time, message and the last lines of the service log.', [], []),
            $k('Which people can see the InterLink Sync page?', 'who sees interlink sync, interlink sync access, interlink sync users, page permissions', 'Users who have access to the InterLink Sync menu item; sending still needs an approved, signed report.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I turn the service off for maintenance?', 'turn service off maintenance, disable service temporarily, maintenance mode service, pause sending', 'Yes: in Settings turn off "Send reports through the background service" so the extension is used meanwhile, or Exit the tray program. Waiting jobs stay saved and continue later.', [], $st),
            $k('What happens to waiting jobs when I turn the service off?', 'jobs after service off, waiting jobs service off, queue when off, jobs kept service exit', 'They stay saved on the service computer and continue in order when the program starts again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does NEXUS-L need to be restarted after Settings changes?', 'restart nexus after settings, apache restart settings, restart needed settings, no restart settings', 'No. Settings are read from the database. Only a database switch is picked up on the next request after it writes .env.', [], $st),
            $k('How do I thank the team?', 'credits, credited by, who built, systems process audit, thanks team', 'Nexus-L InterLink Sender is credited by Systems & Process Audit.', [], []),

            // =========================================================== More quick answers (25)
            $k('What is the quickest way to send a report?', 'quickest way send, fastest send, shortest steps send, simple send steps', 'Open the approved report in InterLink Sync, check the Application No. and Lab Reference, and press Send. Then carry on with other work: the result arrives as a toast and a Synology message.', [], $il + $goIl),
            $k('Do I have to keep the NEXUS-L page open while it sends?', 'keep page open while sending, stay on page, leave page while sending, keep tab open', 'No. The service works on its own on the service computer. You may close the page; the Synology message still arrives.', [], $il),
            $k('What does "service is busy" mean?', 'service is busy, busy message, busy service message, service working other', 'The service is submitting another report. Yours was accepted into the queue and will start in its turn.', [], $il),
            $k('What does the version in the Check result tell me?', 'version in check result, check version meaning, service version check, what version means', 'It is the version of the running service program. If it is lower than the newest setup, update by running the new installer over it.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I install the service on Windows Server?', 'install on windows server, server os service, windows server support, server installation', 'Yes, if the server has a logged-in user session for the tray program and Chrome or Edge installed. The usual choice is a normal Windows 10/11 PC that stays on.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does the installer add a Windows service?', 'installer windows service, add windows service, service in services.msc, windows service entry', 'No. It installs a tray program that starts with Windows. To run without a logged-in user, create a Windows service or scheduled task yourself using the --service option.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Where do I see the program in Windows Apps?', 'see program in apps, installed apps list, apps and features service, uninstall list', 'Settings > Apps > Installed apps > Nexus-L InterLink Service. The publisher shows Systems & Process Audit.', [], $il),
            $k('Can I change the install folder later?', 'change install folder later, move install folder, relocate service, different folder after install', 'Uninstall and install again into the new folder (settings and sign-in are removed by the uninstall, so copy appsettings.Local.json and the data folder first if you want to keep them). Then tick Start with Windows again.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How do I keep my settings when reinstalling?', 'keep settings reinstall, backup settings service, save appsettings before uninstall, keep session reinstall', 'Copy appsettings.Local.json and the data folder before uninstalling, and copy them back after installing. A plain update over the old installation keeps them without copying.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('The Start with Windows entry points to an old folder', 'start with windows old folder, autostart wrong path, run key old path, startup entry wrong', 'Tick Start with Windows again in the service Settings (or reinstall with that option): it rewrites the entry to the current folder.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Which Windows user should run the service?', 'which windows user service, user account service, run as which user, service account windows', 'A dedicated lab user that stays logged in on the service computer. The saved InterLink session belongs to that user\'s program folder.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can the service computer go to sleep?', 'computer sleep service, sleep mode service, power settings service, hibernate service', 'Set the computer to never sleep while plugged in. A sleeping computer cannot receive reports; they fail with "service not reachable".', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What happens after a Windows update restarts the computer?', 'windows update restart service, restart after update, reboot service, after reboot service', 'If Start with Windows is ticked and the user logs in, the service starts again by itself and continues the saved queue. Set the user to log in automatically if nobody does.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Why is the file name NexusInterlinkService-Setup-1.1.0.exe?', 'installer file name, setup file name version, name of setup, setup naming', 'Name of the program, the word Setup and the version, so you can see which version you hold.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the service send emails?', 'service sends email, email notification service, mail from service, interlink email', 'The service itself sends none. InterLink sends its own notification to the recipients in Settings > InterLink report defaults, and NEXUS-L sends the Synology message.', [], $il),
            $k('Does the service work with other InterLink brands?', 'other brands service, other buyers interlink, other brand report, brand not vans', 'It fills the brand, season and package from Settings, so another brand needs those defaults changed to values that exist in InterLink for that brand.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can the service submit a report that is not for this factory?', 'service other factory report, wrong factory submit, factory mismatch', 'The factory values come from Settings. Reports for another factory need their own defaults, otherwise InterLink may refuse the values.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Does the service keep copies of the signed PDF?', 'service keeps pdf copy, pdf copy service, pdf stored service, signed pdf copy', 'It holds the PDF in the job file while the job is queued or running. The original stays in NEXUS-L\'s approvals folder.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can I see the job file contents?', 'job file contents, view queue file, open job json, read queue file', 'The files in data\\queue are JSON with the payload and the PDF. Treat them as report data and do not share them.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('What if I press Send and nothing happens?', 'press send nothing happens, send button no reaction, send does nothing, no message after send', 'Reload the page (Ctrl + F5) and look for a red toast. If there is none, check that the report is approved and that the browser console shows no error; then tell an administrator.', [], $il),
            $k('What if the toast says queued but I never get a result?', 'queued never result, no finished message, stuck queued no result, lost job', 'Look at the Activity window on the service computer: the job is waiting, running or in the history. If it is not there at all, send again; an administrator can check data\\queue and the log.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('How can I tell whether the service is up from NEXUS-L?', 'service up from nexus, service status in nexus, is service running, status indicator service', 'Settings > InterLink service > Test the service shows it. The Send button also tells you at once if the service cannot be reached.', [], $il + $adm),
            $k('Can the service be used from outside the lab network?', 'service from outside, remote access service, internet access service, vpn service', 'It is meant for the local network only. Do not expose its port to the internet; use a VPN if NEXUS-L runs elsewhere.', [], $il + $adm),
